# Catalogue

Editorial strings use `L10nText` (`en` required; any other locale key optional). Resolve `locale → en → first key`. Chrome copy (Play, Settings) belongs in i18next, not the catalogue. Validate JSON with Valibot in `src/catalogue/schema.ts`.

Host: Cloudflare Pages Direct Upload from `Open-Sikh-Apps/gurbani-paath-player-catalogue` (Wrangler CI, not Connect-to-Git). Probe `catalogue.version.json`, then `catalogue.json?v={version}` on mismatch. Validate with the same Valibot schema **in the catalogue repo CI** before upload (checkouts this app and runs `npx tsx scripts/validate-catalogue.ts`). On device: off-thread `JSON.parse` plus a cheap shape check; persist the downloaded text in MMKV (`id: "catalogue"`, `format` key). Do not run full Valibot on device. Refresh on cold start, Home pull-to-refresh, and Home overflow. The app never calls Sanity.

```ts
type L10nText = { en: string; [locale: string]: string };
type L10nUrl = { en: string; [locale: string]: string };

type Author = {
  id: string;
  name: L10nText;
  imageUrl?: string;
  aboutUrl?: L10nUrl;
};

type Reciter = {
  id: string;
  name: L10nText;
  imageUrl?: string; // unused on Paath Home; no Gursikh portraits
  aboutUrl?: L10nUrl;
};

type Scripture = {
  id: string;
  name: L10nText;
  imageUrl?: string;
  aboutUrl?: L10nUrl;
  sttmCoSlug?: string; // https://sttm.co/{sttmCoSlug}/{startAng}
};

type ResourceSection = {
  id: string;
  title: L10nText;
};

type ResourceItem = {
  id: string;
  sectionId: string; // ResourceSection.id
  title: L10nText;
  description: L10nText;
  url: string;
};

type TrackBase = {
  id: string;
  title: L10nText;
  url: string; // https://media.…/audio/{collectionId}/{trackId}.mp3
};

type SehajPaathTrack = TrackBase & {
  kind: "sehaj_paath";
  durationSec: number;
  startAng?: number;
  endAng?: number;
  angTimestamps?: { tSec: number; ang: number }[];
};

type AudiobookTrack = TrackBase & {
  kind: "audiobook";
  durationSec: number;
  readAlongUrl?: string;
};

type RadioTrack = TrackBase & {
  kind: "radio";
};

type Track = SehajPaathTrack | AudiobookTrack | RadioTrack;

type CollectionBase = {
  id: string;
  title?: L10nText;
  authorId?: string;
  languages: string[];
  artworkUrl?: string;
  downloadable: boolean;
};

type SehajPaathCollection = CollectionBase & {
  kind: "sehaj_paath";
  reciterId: string;
  scriptureId: string;
  tracks: SehajPaathTrack[];
};

type AudiobookCollection = CollectionBase & {
  kind: "audiobook";
  reciterId?: string;
  scriptureId?: string;
  tracks: AudiobookTrack[];
};

type RadioCollection = CollectionBase & {
  kind: "radio";
  reciterId?: string;
  scriptureId?: string;
  tracks: RadioTrack[];
};

type Collection = SehajPaathCollection | AudiobookCollection | RadioCollection;

type Catalogue = {
  version: number;
  heroImageUrl: string; // Maharaj's saroop on Home; file on R2
  authors: Author[];
  reciters: Reciter[];
  scriptures: Scripture[];
  collections: Collection[];
  resourceSections: ResourceSection[];
  resources: ResourceItem[];
};
```

Every `id` (Author, Reciter, Scripture, Collection, Track, ResourceSection, ResourceItem) must be unique across the whole catalogue. Prefer UUID.

`durationSec` is required on `sehaj_paath` and `audiobook` tracks. Radio tracks omit it — live streams have no finite length.

V1 Home lists `kind === "sehaj_paath"` only, labeled by reciter, not collection title. `sehaj_paath` requires `reciterId` and `scriptureId`. Keep `kind` / `languages` / `scriptureId` for later filters. Group Resources by `sectionId` → `ResourceSection`.
